INTRO The goal here is to help us figure out what to teach, but we are giving credit for the quiz anyway. The quiz will be graded generously: any good-faith attempt to answer the questions should get full credit. You may _not_ use AI or other reference material for this quiz; if you don't remember something, please just take your best guess! 

SA What are you hoping to learn from this course?

SA Are you currently involved in a research project? Describe it briefly.

SA What statistics or probability courses have you taken as an undergraduate?

SA How would you (personally) _define_ a P value?

SA A classmate tests how plants grow with and without potassium fertilizer. They find that the average growth is higher without fertilizer. How would you (briefly) explain why they should calculate a P value, and how to interpret it?

SA How much experience do you have with organizing files into folders on your computer?

SA How much experience do you have with the R statistics and programming environment?
